{%- doc -%}
Loading banner component that displays a thin progress bar at the top of the page.

This component shows a floating progress bar that fills to 50% during page transitions and completes to 100% when the page is fully loaded. It provides visual feedback for page loading states without blocking the full screen.

@param {string} [class] - Additional CSS classes for the loading bar container
@param {string} [color] - Background color for the progress bar (defaults to 'bg-subtle')
@param {number} [height] - Height of the loading bar in pixels (defaults to 8)
@param {string} [target] - Target element to bind to (defaults to 'body')

@example
{% render '_body-loading-bar' %}

{%- enddoc -%}

<loading-banner
  class="absolute top-0 left-0 h-1 w-full pointer-events-none"
  data-color="bg-neutral-300"
  data-target="{{ target }}"
></loading-banner>

<script src="{{ 'loading-banner.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>